## assemble --help
assemble — composite rendered plates onto the spine, check cuts, add stems and the brand outro, export out/final.mp4

Usage: assemble <project-folder|plates.json> [options]

Reads plates.json, its spine (manifest.json or beatgrid.json) and its brand pack, and the
renders in renders/plates/<id>.mp4. Writes review/review.mp4 (plates on the spine with the
narration at -16 LUFS, or a silent track for a beat grid), fails with the timecode if a plate
cut is not inside a silent gap, remuxes --music/--sfx stems with remux-audio (picture
copied) into review/review-mix.mp4, renders the brand outro once (cached in renders/), and
writes out/final.mp4 = spine + outro, checked with probe-spec. Report: review/assemble.json.

Options:
      --brand <dir>          Brand pack folder (overrides plates.json brand)
      --renders <dir>        Folder of plate renders <id>.mp4 (default: <project>/renders/plates)
      --out <dir>            Where review/, out/ and the outro cache go (default: the project folder)
      --music <file>         Music bed stem, ducked under the narration
      --sfx <file>           SFX stem, already placed on the timeline
      --music-lufs <LUFS>    Music bed loudness before ducking (default: -28)
      --sfx-db <dB>          Gain applied to the SFX stem (default: 0)
      --export <preset>      Final export: source | 1080p60 (source = plates.json size and fps) (default: source)
      --min-silence-ms <ms>  Silent gap every plate cut must sit in (DEC-13) (default: 300)
      --outro <file.mp4>     Use this pre-rendered outro instead of rendering the brand outro
      --rerender-outro       Render the brand outro even if a cached render exists
      --json                 Print the assembly report as JSON
  -h, --help                 Show this help and exit
      --version              Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  assemble my-video/
  assemble my-video/ --music my-video/audio/music.wav --sfx my-video/audio/sfx.wav --export 1080p60
